# Container runtime state vs intelligence output — split policy.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DISCARD (runtime / secrets):
#   data/home/       VNC passwords, X11 cookies, msf history, dnsrecon API keys,
#                    subfinder provider configs, dbus session bus, scapy caches.
#   data/workspace/  Active pentest workspace — transient WIP, can hold anything.
data/home/
data/workspace/

# KEEP (intelligence):
#   data/loot/<ts>/manifest.json   — declarative run record, no raw secrets
#   data/loot/<ts>/report.md       — curated human summary
#
# DISCARD inside data/loot/ (raw artifacts can leak host paths, open ports,
# vuln details, /etc contents, SUID lists, network state):
data/loot/**/*.stderr
data/loot/**/*.stdout
data/loot/**/*.txt
data/loot/**/*.xml
data/loot/**/*.gnmap
data/loot/**/*.nmap
data/loot/**/*.dat
data/loot/**/*.log
data/loot/**/*.pickle
data/loot/**/*.pcap
data/loot/**/*.json
data/loot/**/*.jsonl
data/loot/**/*.conf
# …but unignore the curated summaries:
!data/loot/**/manifest.json
!data/loot/**/report.md
!data/loot/**/safety.md
